{
  "about": "Canonical vectors for the v2 pairing URL grammar. Read by the Rust test `test_pairing_url_vectors_are_honoured` in shared/src/models.rs (via include_str!) and by PairingUrlTest.kt in server-android (the same path, resolved from the Gradle test working directory server-android/app). Both parsers must agree on every case: `accept` says whether the URL is a valid v2 pairing URL, and for an accepted URL the `sid`/`pk`/`port`/`ip4`/`ip6` fields are the values it must yield (null for an absent component). Hex is written in lower case so the Rust side's decode-and-re-encode of `sid` matches the phone's verbatim text, and `ip4`/`ip6` are written in the canonical text `std::net::Ipv4Addr`/`Ipv6Addr`'s `Display` produces, because the Rust side compares `ip.to_string()`: an accepted IPv6 written in any of its accepted spellings yields that one value. Add a case here, never in one suite only.",
